#: ../../source/docs/trolling-motor.rst:5
#: e785749e537b4477a60045cd43f1dbdc
msgid "Trolling Motor"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/trolling-motor.rst:9
#: ae4b550cc29a435d9c67dcf4050487a6
msgid "This articles describes how to set-up a trolling motor for use with Rover"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/trolling-motor.rst:12
#: 267425f237254be9b86ce8e4dcaa0aa5
msgid "What To Buy"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/trolling-motor.rst:14
#: a89d0d92227a4cc3b7ed227bdd9a1750
msgid "Brushed trolling motor like the `Minn Kota Endura C2-30 <https://minnkotamotors.johnsonoutdoors.com/freshwater-trolling-motors/endura-c2>`__.  This can be powered from a 12V lipo battery and draws about 15amps at top speed"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/trolling-motor.rst:15
#: 6eb52134f4064819b914e3383dce06ad
msgid "Brushed motor controller with PWM input like the `Cytron SmartDrive 40 <https://www.cytron.io/p-mds40b>`__ or one of the `RoboClaw brushless motor controllers <http://www.basicmicro.com/34VDC_c_19.html>`__"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/trolling-motor.rst:16
#: aca84d5cbdb540519a6581612b97d5cd
msgid "3S Lipo battery with at least 20C rating and 5000mAh capacity (this should allow running at full speed for about 15min)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/trolling-motor.rst:19
#: 97a44cdc38ff4fcd9e88b9ea3f25956a
msgid "Connecting and Configuring"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/trolling-motor.rst:21
#: 97fd462ab9664bd68d30907333e30716
msgid "Remove the upper handle and control section of the motor to expose the positive and negative leads"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/trolling-motor.rst:22
#: 0e1d2bbd907147d3a49159cdbce21524
msgid "Connect the motor leads to the M1 terminals of the brushed motor controller"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/trolling-motor.rst:23
#: bae87728c6364c4b897e24ddd15270f8
msgid "Connect the motor controller's RC input to the appropriate RC output from the autopilot (i.e. RC Output 3 for a :ref:`Separate Steering and Throttle vehicle <rover-motor-and-servo-connections>`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/trolling-motor.rst:29
#: a4ef2d47203046b695cadc3889c21976
msgid "Test the motor moves in the correct direction using the Mission Planner's Motor Test page (see :ref:`Motor and Servo configuration <rover-motor-and-servo-configuration>` wiki page).  If the motor spins in the incorrect direction then reverse the black and red wires connecting the motor driver to the motor or change the :ref:`SERVO3_REVERSED <SERVO3_REVERSED>` parameter (assuming motor controller is connected to autopilot's RC Output 3)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/trolling-motor.rst:30
#: ff1ebdc1329f48e586d53373e0551fbe
msgid "If the motor does not spin at full speed try lowering :ref:`SERVO3_MIN <SERVO3_MIN>` and/or increasing :ref:`SERVO3_MAX <SERVO3_MAX>` (assuming motor controller is connected to autopilot's RC Output 3)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/trolling-motor.rst:31
#: 7dc200b4f2824e63955675ee80bb38f3
msgid "If the motor moves slowly forwards or backwards when it should be stopped then adjust :ref:`SERVO3_TRIM <SERVO3_TRIM>` (assuming motor controller is connected to autopilot's RC Output 3)"
msgstr ""
